I generated and adjusted this accessibility statement from the [W3C Accessibility Statement Generator Tool](https://www.w3.org/WAI/planning/statements/). I am committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. I am continually improving the user experience for everyone, and applying the relevant accessibility standards.

## Measures to support accessibility

Kitty Giraudel takes the following measures to ensure accessibility of KittyGiraudel.com:

- Include accessibility as part of my mission statement.
- Include accessibility throughout my internal policies.
- Integrate accessibility into my procurement practices.

## Conformance status

The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) defines requirements for designers and developers to improve accessibility for people with disabilities. It defines three levels of conformance: Level A, Level AA, and Level AAA. KittyGiraudel.com is **partially conformant** with WCAG 2.2 level AA. Partially conformant means that some parts of the content do not fully conform to the accessibility standard.

I aim for AA on pages I author and control. I do not claim the whole site, including third-party widgets and older embeds, meets AA with no exceptions.

### Known limitations

- [Site search](/blog/search/) runs entirely in the browser. There is no server-side search, so the form is unusable when JavaScript is disabled or fails to load.
- Comments on blog posts use [Giscus](https://giscus.app/), a GitHub Discussions widget in a third-party iframe. Reading and posting comments requires JavaScript. Posting also requires a GitHub account. I do not control that widget’s accessibility.
- The skip-to-content lives in the desktop site navigation, which is not shown on small screens (below 768px). Keyboard users on those viewports do not get that bypass.

Some older posts include third-party embeds (for example CodePen). Those frames are outside this site’s markup.

## Feedback

I welcome your feedback on the accessibility of this site. Please let me know if you encounter accessibility barriers on [GitHub](https://github.com/KittyGiraudel/site/issues), or [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/kitty-giraudel/).

## Technical specifications

Accessibility of this site relies on the following technologies to work with the particular combination of web browser and any assistive technologies or plugins installed on your computer:

- HTML
- WAI-ARIA
- CSS
- JavaScript

These technologies are relied upon for conformance with the accessibility standards used. Search and comments, as noted above, also depend on JavaScript.
